Lab 03 - Bash Script Review

GenAI Usage

GenAI used

ChatGPT (OpenAI) was used as an AI-assisted editing and learning tool.

Prompts used

The following prompts were used during the lab:

"give me step by step"

"Modify the script so that the user passes a number in and the script tests to see if more than that number of processes are running"

"Exercise 2: Make a copy of the script... modify the script so that instead of writing to the screen, the script writes to a file using the redirect append (>>)"

"Exercise 3: Make a copy of the script... modify the script so that the user can select which of the two behaviours s/he wants"

Code modified after AI suggestions

I used ChatGPT to help understand and modify the Bash scripts.

For Exercise 1, I modified the script to use $1 to accept a number from the command line and used ps -ef | wc -l to count the running processes. I then used an if statement with -gt to compare the process count with the number provided.

For Exercise 2, I changed the echo commands to use >> so that the output was appended to process_log.txt. I also used $(date) to add a date/time stamp to each log entry.

For Exercise 3, I added a menu so the user can choose whether the result is displayed on the screen or written to the log file.

I tested the scripts in the Linux VM and checked the output and log file to make sure they worked as expected.

Reflection on learning

I ensured my learning by following the commands in the Linux VM and testing the scripts myself. I tested the scripts with different input values and choices and checked the contents of the log file. This helped me understand command-line parameters, pipes, if statements, redirect append (>>), and comments in Bash.
